// THE SHIPPED DEFAULT of the cabin (ship homes increment 6). Compiled into the exe
// (src/embedded_data.rs `shipped_home_design`) and never written by the game: a neighbour's
// cabin is drawn as it (src/ship/neighbours.rs), and a game with no data/homes/cabin.ron of its
// own starts its cabin from it. YOUR cabin is data/homes/cabin.ron, which every editor Save
// rewrites; it starts as a copy of this file WITHOUT this paragraph (src/embedded_data.rs
// `own_home_text` drops everything from the first line down to the bare // below).
// To change the cabin every newcomer gets, edit this file (keeping this paragraph on top) and
// rebuild: it is in build.rs FINGERPRINT_INPUTS, so a rig refuses an exe built before the edit.
//
// HumanityOS home design: the CABIN (3.15 x 2.5 m, 7.5 m2 inside its walls), the smallest
// start (data/homes/starts.ron; docs/design/ship-homes-increment-6-plan.md section 3.2). One private
// room on a cabin block's hall: you sleep, keep your things and sit at a desk here, and eat in the
// mess hall and wash in the block's washroom down the hall. It carries NO position on the ship:
// the loader places it at the origin of a plot of kind "cabin" (data/blueprints/ship_structure.ron).
// Home-local metres from the box's min corner (x east, z south).
//
//   kind  "cabin": the plots it fits, and this file's name.
//   door  (0.0, 1.25): the west wall's middle. Every cabin's hall runs along its west side, and
//         every cabin plot's door record must meet this point (the loader checks).
//   body  one room, no interior walls: 3.15 m east to west, 2.5 m north to south, 2.6 m high.
//         Steel shell and a steel ceiling (an inner cabin has no skylight). One ceiling panel in
//         the middle. You arrive a metre inside the door.
//
// Why these numbers. England's Nationally Described Space Standard (Department for Communities
// and Local Government, "Technical housing standards: nationally described space standard",
// March 2015) gives a single bedroom a floor area of at least 7.5 m2 and a width of at least
// 2.15 m, both measured inside the walls, and a minimum floor to ceiling height of 2.3 m. The
// cabin's box is measured to the middle of its walls, and its 0.06 m steel shell, centred on the
// box's edge, takes 0.03 m off each side: 3.15 x 2.5 m outside is 3.09 x 2.44 m inside, 7.54 m2
// and 2.44 m wide. The 2.5 m is the cabins' spacing along their hall (c1 to c16 in
// data/blueprints/ship_structure.ron, 2.5 m apart), so the room grew east to west instead (the
// cabin row, increment 6 lane 1A; the 3.0 x 2.5 m box before it was 7.17 m2 inside). The ceiling
// stands 0.3 m over the standard's 2.3 m, room for the ceiling light. A shared washroom down
// the hall, rather than one in every cabin, follows the shared berthing the design cites (Navy
// Times, 2014-10-13; docs/design/ship-homes-and-logistics.md).
//
// Machines (bed, nightstand, wardrobe, desk, chair, wall screen) are data/machines/cabin.ron.
// Materials: 0 = grid, 1 = steel/metal, 2 = concrete, 3 = wood, 4 = glass.

(
    kind: "cabin",
    door: (0.0, 1.25),
    body: (
        width: 3.15,
        depth: 2.5,
        height: 2.6,
        shell_material: 1,
        roof_material: 1,
        walls: [],
        shell_thickness: None,
        lights: [
            (
                type_id: "ceiling_panel",
                pos: (1.575, 2.45, 1.25),
                dir: (0.0, -1.0, 0.0),
                on: true,
                color: None,
                intensity: None,
                range: None,
                path: [],
                subdivision: 0,
            ),
        ],
        spawn: Some((1.0, 1.25)),
        structures: [],
        road_nodes: [],
        road_edges: [],
        zones: [
            (
                id: "room-cabin",
                type_id: "room_bedroom",
                origin: (0.0, 0.0, 0.0),
                size: (3.15, 2.6, 2.5),
                label: "Cabin",
                room_type: Some("bedroom"),
            ),
        ],
        rail_nodes: [],
        rail_edges: [],
    ),
)
